  "passage": {
    "text": "A shop needs the right amount of stock. If there is too little stock, the product is out of stock and customers go to another shop. If there is too much stock, the goods wait in the warehouse and the company pays for the space. We call this overstock. Every day the manager checks the inventory on the computer. She looks at the demand, so she knows which products people buy fast. When the stock is low, she makes a new order from the supplier. Good stock management saves money and keeps customers happy.",
    "cloze": true,
